.page mktemp 1 create a temporary file or directory

# SYNOPSIS
*mktemp* [*-d*] [_TEMPLATE_]

# DESCRIPTION
`mktemp` creates a new, empty temporary file (mode 0600) and prints its name. The template is a path whose last characters are `X`; they are replaced with random letters and digits. The default template is `/tmp/tmp.XXXXXXXXXX`. The file is created with `O_EXCL`, so two programs can never get the same one.

# OPTIONS
@ *-d*
    Create a directory (mode 0700) instead of a file.

# EXIT STATUS
0, or 1 when the file could not be created.

# EXAMPLES
    f=$(mktemp)
    d=$(mktemp -d /tmp/work.XXXXXX)

# SEE ALSO
touch(1), mkdir(1), rm(1)
